#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171830 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/id #uuid "91f986c6-c305-50eb-a5b7-36043279d128" :question/math-academy-id "e-9505" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$\n\n- $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-2u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171831 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/id #uuid "9779a982-2048-58e2-8a90-df2bcb366d96" :question/math-academy-id "e-9506" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171832 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2ddc4e15-3729-5425-953c-1cb95edc201b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9508" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v+1 \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\, .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de2bb541-e52a-5f01-8123-740252417edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168554} {:answer/id #uuid "0ee6fbd5-0131-512a-aafe-29aa94d6f4a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{1}$ and $T_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168555} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd8680d-d5fa-535b-a007-2fc3cf82791c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168556} {:answer/id #uuid "38087fea-57af-5341-afc5-5c98be6982b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{1}$ and $T_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168557} {:answer/id #uuid "44f3c4af-7197-50a0-b127-0bb285d96b20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38087fea-57af-5341-afc5-5c98be6982b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{1}$ and $T_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168557} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e7c6755-b318-51f4-8a73-5e11986d7717" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168553}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d581310-6942-54b8-b545-b203d0da1352" :question/math-academy-id "q-124007" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2} \\\\ -v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+2 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term ${u}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f09a5f2b-1ad2-54c2-91f8-f8cadcbb12b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168560} {:answer/id #uuid "166b26f4-c78c-560d-a59a-0e8177d66e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168561} {:answer/id #uuid "323ed335-fb2e-5758-84d3-20176fe394ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168562} {:answer/id #uuid "682a4471-d339-5ea0-87c1-699d262d1044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168563} {:answer/id #uuid "685a2114-6880-5ada-9ed5-303b4ca9325a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "685a2114-6880-5ada-9ed5-303b4ca9325a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168564} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebc81363-f353-5c8e-aa70-8e1de58df97a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b49d315-187b-5a70-8690-97b6311cd839" :question/math-academy-id "q-124088" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=u-2v+1,\\,y=u+v-2\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}u-2v+1 \\\\ u+v-2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-2v+1 \\\\ u+v-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-2v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+(-2)=-3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "502d97bc-e3f4-5321-a431-5be31708cdc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295106} {:answer/id #uuid "2458a5a6-4f05-549f-bae1-5f822edbc4a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295107} {:answer/id #uuid "5617311d-a1b3-5e38-883d-8d5e6cd32632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295108} {:answer/id #uuid "00ac6789-8d1e-55c4-8fed-6be8abc04f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295109} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9fa3b0-1490-53e7-8bae-7ed2b110a59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5617311d-a1b3-5e38-883d-8d5e6cd32632" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295108} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1ad6178-be47-5010-ac59-7d77df9bd103" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c24d0407-e7f5-5faf-b383-5febad2af8fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-124236" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ \\sqrt{v}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+1 \\\\ {v}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3u-2 \\\\ 8-v\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\sqrt{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-2 \\\\ 8-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u \\\\ -v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295111 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa1eb52d-5918-531a-847e-e7183292a357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295113} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7f88db-602f-5d13-bd76-b67013a04e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295114} {:answer/id #uuid "4921b728-e559-5950-b1e1-5d48b087121d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295115} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc8898e-b8a2-5834-92d5-7b2cacef4d9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295116} {:answer/id #uuid "62384ace-b84c-5e85-95f4-b664393de08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa7f88db-602f-5d13-bd76-b67013a04e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295114} :answer-field/id #uuid "9adf5d47-b90f-57ec-9563-b1300c861940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7c49d1f-62c6-5240-9ecd-d0ff7b646237" :question/math-academy-id "q-124247" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 1-{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u(v-1) \\\\ u-1\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c79024cd-3162-5ca1-a28c-754210b033b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295120} {:answer/id #uuid "e4308fce-14c2-5c2f-8538-954f1e414076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295121} {:answer/id #uuid "9c22c731-c074-56e5-a629-c9288315265c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295122} {:answer/id #uuid "7afdf1f1-9d26-54e6-8f12-a584bef92886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295123} {:answer/id #uuid "f57408a6-63e2-5426-970d-c944839a3494" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4308fce-14c2-5c2f-8538-954f1e414076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295121} :answer-field/id #uuid "daab3d87-c882-5ab1-9bb5-b3576fc2dc43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295119}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "147c9fd2-3bca-542f-a5bb-2da2f3c71aff" :question/math-academy-id "q-124251" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic terms ${u}^{2}$ and ${v}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4u+6v \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295125 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "035a4ded-7b92-5073-a8aa-3ffa47aff9ea" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Affine Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f585c66-0570-5c00-9d93-8acb8a3e506e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295127} {:answer/id #uuid "ac90f967-da15-5704-9665-c9929cd922e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295128} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f73f23-5f24-5207-95b5-1a3853e0f1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295129} {:answer/id #uuid "4456ce1b-97eb-545d-b767-dd68122091aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295130} {:answer/id #uuid "750596c5-9b6f-5472-a950-f0c1ea73740f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f585c66-0570-5c00-9d93-8acb8a3e506e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295127} :answer-field/id #uuid "482bb424-6613-54b7-891f-74ee4de3f263" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "111538d1-a3c4-5a8b-bb3b-b571c7d190d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-124253" :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ {e}^{v}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{aligned}]$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the exponential term ${e}^{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295132 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "761e281b-e631-5212-a160-f8db9cbeaac5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295134} {:answer/id #uuid "38946076-2c0f-5674-80f6-7effeb0eb079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295135} {:answer/id #uuid "269d906d-77b3-5906-989e-e1566c26e416" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295136} {:answer/id #uuid "822087bb-8c5c-53ed-ba35-dc591995de18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295137} {:answer/id #uuid "8b254214-745b-583a-bc64-6e5f547d1b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b254214-745b-583a-bc64-6e5f547d1b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295138} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3cbccf9-50b4-50d4-af0b-6b7102c9915e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fbd649a-72ec-5c96-b929-3b7a8cd0013b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124259" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv+3,\\,y=-9u+cv+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ -9u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3 \\\\ -9u+4v+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+0v+3,\\,y=-9u+4v+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+4=5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be48af4-b946-5e8b-ab28-4f792a31a974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295141} {:answer/id #uuid "5e9d9ce5-d759-57bf-80a9-b7ceff4906fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295142} {:answer/id #uuid "f870ced9-0883-5ba8-8e7f-2d7ff9a791bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295143} {:answer/id #uuid "2180f3a8-6e9c-5b8a-af2d-60e6a57d55c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295144} {:answer/id #uuid "6d9683bb-89bc-5459-b095-601993cf9cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f870ced9-0883-5ba8-8e7f-2d7ff9a791bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295143} :answer-field/id #uuid "0df96ffa-72ad-5985-a938-cb8d42f45297" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42e18668-b4ac-5ec0-a619-27855b78e8aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-124261" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+bv-2,\\,y=u+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+8v \\\\ u\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+8v-2 \\\\ u+5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=6u+8v-2,\\,y=u+5\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+8+5=19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d263d41b-4aa6-5a6d-904f-b9908b92d41b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295148} {:answer/id #uuid "de71996b-991c-5da0-b670-c1c679e5ab55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295149} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3019ef-c11f-501f-943c-967172209bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295150} {:answer/id #uuid "19263934-97bc-5927-a5db-ca4465c70a06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295151} {:answer/id #uuid "eb867a84-baac-5fa5-8a08-207368d5d554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc3019ef-c11f-501f-943c-967172209bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295150} :answer-field/id #uuid "09727357-b546-5ddc-a1ed-bc46ae26aaf8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295147}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9eda2acd-bd7f-59a7-882f-5daee5afa9d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124262" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+v,\\,y=bu+cv\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2u+v \\\\ 9u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2u+v \\\\ 9u+3v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-2u+v,\\,y=9u+3v\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+9+3=10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295153 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "586d374d-19a9-5e0d-a493-3fdc56821f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295155} {:answer/id #uuid "680e04a0-0629-5a21-8300-9ee6428bb691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295156} {:answer/id #uuid "de3d719c-ecae-5572-ab31-32df6daee9ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295157} {:answer/id #uuid "058c02f9-4194-5198-a0e0-9d4156223fa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295158} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d07946-66ab-53a5-80c3-8523b15a8e06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "586d374d-19a9-5e0d-a493-3fdc56821f84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295155} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c8e513a-57cd-5022-b067-355accbb231e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "668b8cce-7490-551f-a33e-78d7ea6e33f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-124263" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4u+av-2,\\,y=bu+cv-3\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-v \\\\ 9u+5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-v-2 \\\\ 9u+5v-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=4u+(-1)v-2,\\,y=9u+5v-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+9+5=13.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172229 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6664fc2f-f776-5da1-823a-c5ab35873e51" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Matrix Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3dc5605-ef7f-518e-b1e3-20954b09c8ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168578} {:answer/id #uuid "350f4c0f-fd12-5a8d-89d2-6366c1bf14eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168579} {:answer/id #uuid "4b773b7b-8eff-5cff-a441-966c14c9765a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168580} {:answer/id #uuid "698a714f-db57-5ba0-8a40-8f3e4aac0d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168581} {:answer/id #uuid "7810f291-2b7a-57b3-ab5a-0230e08951c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "698a714f-db57-5ba0-8a40-8f3e4aac0d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168581} :answer-field/id #uuid "7304f343-c0bb-5a33-8c0c-688d4eb5bda6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9882bc48-ffe2-5a96-827b-d1eb44c92577" :question/math-academy-id "q-124271" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=au+4v,\\,y=-5u+bv+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3u+4v \\\\ -5u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3u+4v \\\\ -5u+3v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-3u+4v,\\,y=-5u+3v+0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-3+3+0=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62ccceb4-6067-5bce-b982-d96ab19ee9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295162} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b35623-d326-5fb9-91ba-e8f93b1fe7db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295163} {:answer/id #uuid "ec74b222-bfdc-5fd9-9901-d062abb31c9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295164} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8d000c-d154-5174-9dc0-69d3a40286ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295165} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9ac776-4ed0-511c-a57a-d8c2c9d6502c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62ccceb4-6067-5bce-b982-d96ab19ee9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295162} :answer-field/id #uuid "879f4cc5-b9a7-5a26-b6f3-bc229be46c40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94ef537c-d453-5e44-8027-fc902bea1259" :question/math-academy-id "q-124284" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4v-u,\\,y=3v-7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4v-u \\\\ 3v-7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v \\\\ 3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+4+0=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "373f8f6b-b1ad-57d5-ad02-6acbef1341c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169} {:answer/id #uuid "8e14f16e-9b4e-58f1-906b-1eee902250fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295170} {:answer/id #uuid "38e23b92-2a75-5dfc-bdf4-513200c83294" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295171} {:answer/id #uuid "1edbfb1c-9a04-5adb-89fb-bf120ffd3ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295172} {:answer/id #uuid "f61e3520-7d0e-5c7c-96cf-a5c357e7b01d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "373f8f6b-b1ad-57d5-ad02-6acbef1341c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295169} :answer-field/id #uuid "313376e7-eb16-55f0-8f6e-6a40eb0fdbb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb3e7867-83ca-5695-bc9b-8585b1f7a576" :question/math-academy-id "q-124285" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u-3v-2,\\,y=2u+v+7\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v-2 \\\\ 2u+v+7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u-3v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+(-2)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "767d66b3-a32b-5cfc-8912-dd84a11b4558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295176} {:answer/id #uuid "c0574db5-6e94-57f2-a4bc-47c808f34672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295177} {:answer/id #uuid "e781ca73-8931-5820-84b5-42d3733c1021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295178} {:answer/id #uuid "88468f42-8f26-58a3-9d2d-bbced21e8085" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295179} {:answer/id #uuid "a3509ded-08be-548b-a69c-a0c07badf2b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "767d66b3-a32b-5cfc-8912-dd84a11b4558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295176} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6fcb877-5357-580c-ad8d-dcca915df97d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1929909-0b5b-54c9-9fb9-14654387893d" :question/math-academy-id "q-124292" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=3v-8u,\\,y=3u-v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & 3 \\\\ b & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3v-8u \\\\ 3u-v\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3v-8u \\\\ 3u-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8u+3v \\\\ 3u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-8+3+0=-5.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5492cc5-8266-527b-b2cf-8d5f5fdc432f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295183} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe44c9c-07b3-55d3-820f-f382ef124b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295184} {:answer/id #uuid "521bba8c-2428-52ba-852a-ac6683eb7c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295185} {:answer/id #uuid "0441e29b-bd6e-54e6-9755-0a4053ddb78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295186} {:answer/id #uuid "2f0a6c11-c265-5864-bb98-df70fe7d2d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f0a6c11-c265-5864-bb98-df70fe7d2d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295187} :answer-field/id #uuid "03a507a4-26f1-59b0-af28-c13d74c534ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27624eaf-a41b-5122-b27f-be42134ea00b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124301" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=6u-v,\\,y=2u-3v+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & -1 \\\\ 2 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+(-3)+4=7.\n$$"}]}
